From 5f4914f326dbf1a5aaae2c6881a743323fb87584 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 12:51:23 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 10/40] clk: exynos: add the remaining CMU blocks of the
 Exynos9820

The driver started with the three blocks storage needs.  Five more are
added here, each one because something the boot loader does now cannot be
reached without it: CMU_FSYS0A for the USB controller, CMU_PERIS for the
system timer, CMU_APM and CMU_CMGP for the low power island the main PMIC
answers from, and CMU_DPU for the display block that draws the menu.

A missing CMU does not announce itself.  The device that needs it simply
never probes, and the failure shows up somewhere else entirely: fastboot
was dead for a while because CMU_FSYS0A was not there, and nothing in the
log mentioned a clock.

The register offsets and the parent of every clock come from the vendor's
calibration tables, not from another port; the port repository checks both
against those tables on every run.

Signed-off-by: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/clk/exynos/clk-exynos9820.c | 1307 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 1259 insertions(+), 48 deletions(-)

